    {
      "name": "Note: wiring and swap",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "parameters": {
        "content": "**Trigger:** POST `{from, to, called_at, call_status}` to this webhook when a call is missed. A phone provider's call-status callback (for example Twilio's voice status callback) can be pointed at it. Calls from withheld numbers, from numbers on the never-text list or the STOP list are ignored; one text per caller per 15 minutes; every handled call becomes a row in `leads` and the owner is alerted.\n\n**Swapping the stand-in for a real SMS service (Twilio, ClickSend, MessageMedia):** in the \"Config\" node change `sms_api_url` to the provider's send-message URL, then on each \"Send ...\" HTTP Request node attach that provider's credential (an n8n credential you create, shown here as \"SMS provider (replace me)\") and adjust the JSON field names (`to`, `from`, `body`) to the provider's. The checks, duplicate handling and logging around it do not change.\n\nThe owner email uses an n8n SMTP credential shown as \"Email (replace me)\".",
        "width": 700,
        "height": 300,
        "color": 7
      },
      "id": "f13d66b4-6a78-005f-e749-7b57cc752084",
      "position": [
        0,
        -400
      ]
    },
